text:
I reviewed the full repo. Overall: compact, readable, and the existing tests are meaningful, but I would not approve it for renewed active development as-is. The main blocker is URL/path construction: IDs are inserted directly into paths, so reserved characters can alter the request target. I also found retry behavior gaps that will matter in production SDK usage.

Verification: after installing `httpx` outside the read-only repo, `PYTHONPATH=/work python -m pytest -q` passed: 32 passed. The workspace is read-only, so pytest emitted a cache warning, and `git` is not available in the container.

